WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.529
So in the US all these changes took
place mostly in the first half of the

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:08.880
20th century, a little beyond. And so
they're basically invisible to us now,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.719
which is why we look at our food system
and we think it's normal, but we're

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:17.550
actually seeing a food system that is
completely distorted by refrigeration.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:23.100
And what's interesting is if you go to a
place that has only just refrigerated or

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.720
is still refrigerating, you can see those
shifts take place. Which is why I went to

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:37.980
China to visit the the factory of
the frozen dumpling mogul who brought

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:43.680
frozen food to China. This is the frozen
dumpling factory. He was a surgeon and

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:50.190
when Deng Xiaoping said, "Oh, you know some
people are going to get rich," this

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:55.680
surgeon decided he would like to be one
of those. And so he harvested some parts

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.649
from some of the hospital machinery and
built a freezer system. He was already

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:06.290
famous in the neighborhood for his
homemade dumplings, and he just started a

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:13.439
a dumpling factory. But what's amazing is
when you go there you can see the same

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:17.580
things play out that played out here. So
there was an issue

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.110
initially, a very intense distrust, and
there still is amongst a certain

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:27.689
generation when I talk to folks about:
could refrigerated and frozen food

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:33.030
be good? Could it really be okay? And
the frozen dumpling mogul told me that

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.680
actually the drip right there on the
dumpling is very important. That

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.180
signified freshness. They tried to sell
the dumplings in a package without

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:47.729
the drip, and they weren't selling
and the drip somehow sort of

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:55.770
communicated a freshness to folks.  I visited people who are

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:00.960
breeding Chinese vegetables to be cold
storage-tolerant, so their vegetables are

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.850
changing in real-time, their diets are
changing, where things are grown is

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.690
changing. This is a big Chinese
government project called the South-to-

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:13.050
North Vegetable Transfer that is
shifting

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:19.260
where things are grown. These are Chinese
apples going out to the world. It's

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:25.170
changing where food is sold, so wet
markets are turning into Walmarts, and

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:30.720
that changes how often people shop. It
changes the layout of their houses. It

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.040
changes the layout of cities. So you
could see all of those things kind of

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.650
changing in real-time. And what's crazy
about China is, so in 2010, the Chinese

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:46.050
government made refrigeration part
of their 12th Five-Year Plan. They were

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:52.710
like, "We are going to refrigerate." And
being China, they just did it. And so it

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:59.880
has, in the past 10 years, the amount of
refrigerated space in China has grown by

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:06.420
more than 20 times. It's just
exploded. And yet still, Chinese people

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:11.190
have less than a third of the cold
storage space of an average American per

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:15.840
capita. So it's still happening. And it's
happening now in India and it's

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.280
happening with Chinese funding in Africa.
So the world is refrigerating at speed.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.720
And a lot of people are like, "Well, this
is a good thing," right? Because diets

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:30.750
improve, people have access to fresh
vegetables and dairy and more animal

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:36.060
protein. That's exciting.
Farmers are not stuck selling all their

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:42.720
harvests when it comes in. They can
export, they can make money.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.620
And then the big thing
that people say is, well, food waste, right?

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.370
When you don't have a cold chain, you
lose a lot of food. So in a country like

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.470
India, where there isn't a robust cold
chain and estimates are that at

00:03:55.470 --> 00:04:01.380
least 40% is lost at
the farm stage, basically before it ever

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:07.709
gets anywhere close to the consumer. In
America, where we have an amazing cold

00:04:07.709 --> 00:04:14.910
chain, well we waste 40 percent on the
consumer end. So the cold chain people,

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:19.799
refrigeration boosters like to say it
prevents food waste, but I think it's a

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:24.360
little more nuanced than that. It kind of
just shifts where it happens. And maybe

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.729
makes it easier to fix? I don't know,
maybe not. This actually strikes me as

00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:32.080
harder to fix in a lot of ways.

